The endpoint returns a single JSON object with these fields:

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `dispatch_enabled` | boolean | Whether the dispatch engine is running |
| `active_invocations` | array | Currently running agent invocations |
| `queue_depth` | number | Number of queued invocations |
| `agent_definitions` | array | Configured agent definitions |

### agent_definitions Array Structure

Each agent definition object contains:

| Field | Type | Source |
|-------|------|--------|
| `id` | string | `a.id` from meta.agents |
| `name` | string | `a.name` from meta.agents |
| `adapter` | string | `a.adapter ?? 'claude-agent-acp'` (defaults to claude-agent-acp) |

### active_invocations Array Structure

Each active invocation object contains:

| Field | Type | Source |
|-------|------|--------|
| `session_id` | string | `inv.sessionId` |
| `agent_id` | string | `inv.agentId` |
| `task_ref` | string \| null | `inv.taskRef ?? null` |
| `elapsed_ms` | number | `inv.elapsedMs` |

The endpoint gracefully handles missing agent definitions by returning an empty array if metadata loading fails.

